   "evidence": "File header lines 8-10: `public import Physlib.Relativity.PauliMatrices.Basic` / `import PhyslibAlpha.Relativity.PauliMatrices.SelfAdjoint`; `upstream/Physlib/PhyslibAlpha/Relativity/PauliMatrices/SelfAdjoint.lean:8` `public import Physlib.Relativity.PauliMatrices.SelfAdjoint`, `:72` `lemma sum_pauliLower_mul_pauliLower`. Every other extension module in `EpsilonEridani/Relativity/` (e.g. `Fermions/Weyl/MetricExtensions.lean`, `SL2C/BasicExtensions.lean`) imports only its own mirrored upstream module.",
   "file": "EpsilonEridani/Relativity/PauliMatrices/BasicExtensions.lean",
   "fix": "Rename/move the module to `EpsilonEridani/Relativity/PauliMatrices/SelfAdjointExtensions.lean` with `public import PhyslibAlpha.Relativity.PauliMatrices.SelfAdjoint` as its first import (dropping the now-implied `Physlib.Relativity.PauliMatrices.Basic` and the separate private import), and update the importers (`EpsilonEridani/QFT/QCD/SU2Generators.lean`, `EpsilonEridani/QuantumMechanics/AngularMomentum/SpinHalf.lean`). If `sum_pauliMatrix_inr_mul_self` is to stay Basic-appendable, keep just that lemma in a `BasicExtensions.lean`.",
   "issue": "The `*Extensions` name/path marks this as material to be appended to `Physlib.Relativity.PauliMatrices.Basic`, but `sum_pauliMatrix_inr_apply_mul_pauliMatrix_inr_apply` and `sum_tensorProductMap_toEuclideanLin_pauliMatrix_inr` are derived from `PauliMatrix.sum_pauliLower_mul_pauliLower`, stated in `PhyslibAlpha/Relativity/PauliMatrices/SelfAdjoint.lean:72`, which itself imports `Physlib.Relativity.PauliMatrices.SelfAdjoint` and hence `Basic`. Appended to `Basic.lean` the file would create an import cycle, so the mirrored-path contract (`upstream module as first import, so the whole file can move`) is not met; the completeness relation's canonical home is beside the Fierz relation it specialises.",
